ibmveth: fix RX poll hang, reopen hang and netpoll races

Hi,

Four fixes for the ibmveth driver. They apply to net-next as is and
do not depend on the two open() error-path fixes recently applied to
net (af0524bf4ce1, 84bec0bf0352); patch 2 explains how it relates to
them. The failures are severe: patches 2 and 4 hang the system
(napi_disable() with RTNL held, or a CPU stuck in poll until RCU
stalls), and patches 1 and 3 fix a NULL dereference, PHYP writing
into an unmapped buffer, and a use-after-free.

They target net-next rather than net: the triggers are rare (an
open() failure during a direct reopen, PHYP returning a bad
correlator, netconsole during a reconfiguration or under TX
contention, a bad RX slot during remove) and there are no field
reports. All four carry Fixes: tags and are suitable for stable once
merged; I can repost them against net if you prefer.

Patches 2 and 4 were requested by the netdev AI review of v7 of
the ibmveth multi-queue RX series, which asked for these fixes to be
split out of it with Fixes: tags:
https://lore.kernel.org/netdev/cover.1790319558.git.mmc@linux.ibm.com/
Patches 1 and 3 came out of the follow-up review of the same code.
Taking all four ahead of the multi-queue series also makes it
smaller: the netpoll, reopen and bad-slot handling become existing
behaviour that it extends per queue.

Patch 1 fixes two ways netpoll reaches RX replenish unsafely.
ndo_poll_controller ran replenish outside NAPI with no lock, racing
NAPI's replenish on the same pool, so a free slot could be posted to
PHYP twice; it is removed, since netpoll polls NAPI itself, as was
done for ibmvnic. And open() enabled NAPI before the RX resources
existed, so netpoll could replenish unallocated pools during the
driver's direct close()/open() pairs; NAPI is now enabled last.

Patch 2 stops a second close() after a failed direct reopen.
change_mtu, the pool sysfs store, set_csum and set_tso close and
reopen the device directly; if that open() fails, IFF_UP stays set
and the next ndo_stop napi_disable()s an already-disabled NAPI with
RTNL held. The hang is deterministic once open() has failed, and it
also blocks shutdown.

Patch 3 disables the reset work before unregister in remove(), so a
reset queued from NAPI in between, for example on a bad RX
correlator, cannot run on a freed adapter.

Patch 4 makes poll step past a bad RX correlator. Since
2c91e2319ed9 turned the correlator BUG_ON()s into WARN_ON() plus a
reset, poll breaks out without advancing the ring and keeps
restarting on the same slot. The reset it schedules is queued on
that CPU and cannot run, and the CPU stalls RCU. A correlator
naming an inactive buffer pool also passed the check and
dereferenced a NULL skbuff array in softirq; it is now treated as
bad too. The WARN_ON()s on PHYP-supplied data become a ratelimited
error, and the dropped frames are counted in rx_dropped.

Each commit message says how the bug was found and how the fix was
tested. In short: the ibmveth KUnit suite on qemu pseries (ppc64le)
passes, and the new cases in patch 4 fail on the unfixed driver. On
a POWER10 LPAR: netconsole under a printk flood and a ping flood,
MTU and buffer pool changes under traffic, a forced open() failure
on an MTU change followed by down and up, and unbind/bind under
traffic.

Thanks,
